IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-6.l4 -- ARTICLE 6(1) AND (2): LAWFULNESS OF PROCESSING.  Layer 1 (P1).  Paragraphs (3) and (4)
-- are in P1-art-6b.l4.
-- Article 6(1) says processing is lawful ONLY IF AND TO THE EXTENT THAT at least one of six points
-- applies.  Each point is a function over the facts; `Art 6(1)` combines the six answers.
-- THE COMBINATION ANSWERS "the condition is met", NOT "the processing is lawful": other provisions
-- (Art 5(1)(a), 7, 8, 9, 10, and national law) add conditions of their own.
-- Whose duty: the condition binds the controller's choice of basis; the data subject may rely on it.
-- Borrowed facts (plain inputs, PLAN.md section 4): consent (Art 4(11)), child (not defined), necessity.
-- "to the extent": each point is asked of one processing operation (the case's natural unit), so the
-- extent is all or nothing (fork F6-1 in NOTES.md).
-- A failed point answers JUST FALSE by an inference from "only if ... at least one of the following
-- applies", clause by clause (marginal reading (a) for a lawyer, NOTES.md).
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 6(1)(a): consent`

-- src:88 | 1. Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies:
-- src:89 | (a) the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data for one or more specific purposes;
@ref Art 6(1)(a) (src:88-89)
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent is for one or more specific purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is for one of those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1)(a) point (a) applies: the data subject has given consent to the processing for one or more specific purposes` MEANS
    IF `the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data`
       AND `the consent is for one or more specific purposes`
       AND `the processing is for one of those purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only if ... applies"): "Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies: (a) the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data for one or more specific purposes"

§ `Article 6(1)(b): contract`

-- src:88 | 1. Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies:
-- src:90 | (b) processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party or in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract;
@ref Art 6(1)(b) (src:88-90)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is necessary in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is necessary for a contract with the data subject or for steps before one` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party`
       OR `the processing is necessary in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only if ... applies"): "(b) processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party or in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract"

§ `Article 6(1)(c): legal obligation`

-- src:88 | 1. Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies:
-- src:91 | (c) processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which the controller is subject;
@ref Art 6(1)(c) (src:88-91)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller is subject to that legal obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1)(c) point (c) applies: the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which the controller is subject` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation` AND `the controller is subject to that legal obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only if ... applies"): "(c) processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which the controller is subject"
    -- Art 6(3) adds that the basis must be laid down by Union law or Member State law: see P1-art-6b.l4.

§ `Article 6(1)(d): vital interests`

DECLARE `Art 6(1)(d) whose vital interests` IS ONE OF
    `Art 6(1)(d) the data subject's`
    `Art 6(1)(d) another natural person's`
    `Art 6(1)(d) the interests of something that is not a natural person`

-- src:88 | 1. Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies:
-- src:92 | (d) processing is necessary in order to protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person;
@ref Art 6(1)(d) (src:88-92)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary in order to protect vital interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whose vital interests` IS AN `Art 6(1)(d) whose vital interests`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1)(d) point (d) applies: the processing is necessary in order to protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary in order to protect vital interests`
       AND NOT (`whose vital interests` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(d) the interests of something that is not a natural person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only if ... applies"): "(d) processing is necessary in order to protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person"

§ `Article 6(1)(e): public interest and official authority`

-- src:88 | 1. Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies:
-- src:93 | (e) processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller;
@ref Art 6(1)(e) (src:88-93)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is necessary in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1)(e) point (e) applies: the processing is necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest`
       OR `the processing is necessary in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only if ... applies"): "(e) processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller"
    -- Art 6(3) adds that the basis must be laid down by Union law or Member State law: see P1-art-6b.l4.

§ `Article 6(1)(f): legitimate interests`

-- src:88 | 1. Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies:
-- src:94 | (f) processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party, except where such interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data, in particular where the data subject is a child.
-- src:95 | Point (f) of the first subparagraph shall not apply to processing carried out by public authorities in the performance of their tasks.
@ref Art 6(1)(f) and the second subparagraph (src:88-95)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject is a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is carried out by a public authority in the performance of its tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the processing is carried out by a public authority in the performance of its tasks`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative): "Point (f) of the first subparagraph shall not apply to processing carried out by public authorities in the performance of their tasks."
        IF NOT (`the processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only if ... applies"): "(f) processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party"
        IF `those interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "except where"): "except where such interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        -- `the data subject is a child` is not read: "in particular where the data subject is a child" points at a case where the interests of the data subject weigh heavily; it does not itself say they override (fork F6-2 in NOTES.md).

§ `Article 6(1): at least one of points (a) to (f)`

-- src:88 | 1. Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies:
@ref Art 6(1), the chapeau (src:88-88)
GIVEN `point (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `point (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `point (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `point (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `point (e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `point (f)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) the condition is met that at least one of points (a) to (f) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `point (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `point (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `point (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `point (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `point (e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `point (f)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `point (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `point (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `point (c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `point (d)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `point (e)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `point (f)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only if"): "Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no point applies yet and at least one point's answer is not covered, so the text does not say that none applies

§ `Article 6(2): Member State provisions for points (c) and (e)`

-- src:96 | 2. Member States may maintain or introduce more specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation with regard to processing for compliance with points (c) and (e) of paragraph 1 by determining more precisely specific requirements for the processing and other measures to ensure lawful and fair processing including for other specific processing situations as provided for in Chapter IX.
@ref Art 6(2) (src:96)
GIVEN `the basis of the processing` IS AN `Art 6(1) lawful basis`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2) a Member State may maintain or introduce more specific provisions to adapt the application of this Regulation to the processing` MEANS
    IF `the basis of the processing` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation`
       OR `the basis of the processing` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "with regard to processing for compliance with points (c) and (e) of paragraph 1"; for the other four bases the text does not say
